{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521468-maryland-and-baltimore-in-mage","id":1521468,"title":"Maryland, and Baltimore, in Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-27T08:19:44-07:00","id":1521468,"title":"Maryland, and Baltimore, in Mage","content":"I am planning an all Ecstatic campaign which will focus in Maryland; I was struggling with where to put it when I came across some stuff about the John Hopkins research facility on psychedelics based in Baltimore. That sounds like a Cult of Ecstacy kind of idea.<br /> <br /> But I've never been to Baltimore. Anyone want to share some things that I should consider in such a campaign? (No, &quot;Go to Baltimore&quot; is not an option.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26003-richard-the-lyin-heart","name":"Richard the Lyin' Heart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T10:57:33-07:00","id":1521473,"title":"","content":"I know there's been some stuff on the city in WoD but I believe it's all VtM so I doubt it will be of much help. So you'd probably be better off reading the city's Wikipedia page to get an idea of major places in the city and thinking about how they'd be useful for Mages and then creating some stuff for them.<br /> <br /> Like the John Hopkins idea you have. Though I'd add to it that the facility is under Technocrat influence because of course it would and the CofX is operating in secret under noses. Seeking to undermine them while also keeping a low profile lest they caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T11:36:22-07:00","id":1521475,"title":"","content":"Washington DC was covered in a Vampire book. Basically, a Lasombra Prince (hidden, people think he's Ventrue) rules the city. The Technocracy, the Unseelie Changelings, and a very small number of Werewolves, also have some power in the City. The Sabbat and the Camarilla are still fighting for control of the Boston to Charlotte NC corridor. The Fianna Werewolves (who have been brutally Flanderized) are influential in the Area. This was good earlier on, it's bad now. The Glass Walkers, the Bone Gnawlers, the Uktena, and the Black Furys, should all be important too.<br /> <br /> The Changeling book <b>Kingdom of the Willows </b>covers Maryland. I think I saw a Black Dog book on Baltimore. Either that or the Sabbat Vampires are supposed to run the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-27-2023, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T12:56:35-07:00","id":1521477,"title":"","content":"While I don't live in Baltimore, it's one of the closer major cities to me, I have a lot of friends in that area, and so on.<br /> <br /> First off, John's Hopkins kinda has to be a Progenitor operation. The place is a very well disguised fortress dedicated to keeping the rest of the Baltimore out. It's like Central Park in NYC, but with multiple layers of security to make sure that nobody that makes less than $50K a year is allowed in without special permission or as service staff. It is the most CoX unfriendly place you can imagine in how utterly superficial anything &quot;good&quot; about it is besides medical research. Now, don't get me wrong, the medical part is fantastic and I'm glad we have it in our world, but it's not a source of pride for the people forced to live next to it. For a different analogy, it's kinda like Vatican City being it's own country inside the city of Rome. It's that drastic of a cultural difference.<br /> <br /> Second, Baltimore is a very difficult city to represent accurately without going there. Yeah, that's pretty true of most cities, but it Baltimore is a set in stone thing, just be straight up with your players that you're going to be doing some research to try to do the city justice, but it's a fictional city based on Baltimore and it's going to depart heavily from reality. To try to help put this in some perspective to help get my point across: the city of Baltimore (not including the greater metro area) is about 81 square miles, with less than 600K residents, with over <b><i>250</i></b>neighborhoods. It's also nearly 300 years old, which by US standards is very old, and thus the layout of the city is a tangled mess of expansions. When you get away from the Inner Harbor (that is, the central tourist and business area) it turns into a maze of what kind of neighborhood you're navigating through. There's a reason they built The Loop (a connected set of highway interchanges that encircles the city and connects all of the outlying suburbs) so it never actually touches the city itself; The Loop is there so people get go around the city to get somewhere else despite the city itself being a major transport hub.<br /> <br /> Third, however cliched this might be thanks to the city being the setting for a bunch of shows, you cannot avoid racism and crime and have an authentic story about modern Baltimore. The White Flight to the 'burbs on The Loop trashed the economies of all those tiny minority neighborhoods, while gentrification spreading from the Inner Harbor continues to choke out any local businesses that don't service the money machine... which unsurprisingly has lead to high crime rates. I know I'm painting a pretty negative picture here. I don't go to to Baltimore as some sort of perverse poverty tourist. But enjoying the rich cultural heritage of the city, getting away from the hype-tourist traps, and so on means coming face-to-face with an extremely bifurcated city of haves and have-nots. Even if you're going with a fictionalized/stylized take on the city to account for having to do your research online... there's no point to picking Baltimore as a city if you're also going to try to ignore how disparate experiences of the city get just by walking a few blocks in a given direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T13:54:03-07:00","id":1521478,"title":"","content":"As far as research, David Simon's work is pretty good. He was a reporter with the Baltimore Sun for over a decade and wrote two non-fiction books about the city, <i>Homicide: A Year on the Killing Streets</i> and <i>The Corner: A Year in the Life of an Inner-City Neighborhood</i>. The first was the basis for the 90s NBC drama <i>Homicide</i> and the second was adapted into an HBO miniseries. Simon later went on to help create the HBO series <i>The Wire</i> and help adapt fellow Sun reporter Justin Fenton's book <i>We Own This City</i> (about the corruption in the Baltimore PD's gun trace task force) into an HBO miniseries. Collectively, they give you an interesting look at the evolution of Baltimore's inner city and police over the past three decades.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T19:49:58-07:00","id":1521569,"title":"","content":"When I think of BMore, Mage: the Ascension doesn't cross my mind; Vampire: Masquerade, the Foresaken: Yes; mage, no. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Richard the Lyin' Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521468-maryland-and-baltimore-in-mage#post1521468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .(No, &quot;Go to Baltimore&quot; is not an option.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? I did, on a whim, visit BMore by bus. Though, I was in Virginia, and I had already traveled cross-country by bus. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}